    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Halnon Humphreys are delighted to present this exceptional opportunity to purchase a 2 bedroom end of terrace town centre property situated within a low density gated development. \r\n\r\nThe property also benefits from having a full grant of planning permission for a side extension which would add two further bedrooms on the first floor and additional living space on the ground floor. \r\n\r\nShould the property be extended, this would increase the floor area by a further 48 sq m/516 sq ft to approx. 140 sq metres.\r\n\r\nThe property achieves an energy rating of B3 and there are a number of items included in the sale which include blinds, curtains, washing machine, dishwasher, fridge freezer, oven, hob, extractor fan and all light fittings.\r\n\r\nThe Laurels is one of the most sought after locations in Gorey due to its proximity to amenities. It is situated in a small, gated development of just 4 houses adjacent to Gorey Hospital and it is a short stroll to Gorey Main Street, Tesco, restaurants and schools to name but a few. \r\n\r\nThere is a private yard/patio area to the front, rear and side of the house which provides for additional parking space.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nGorey is just 50 minutes from the M50 and South Dublin, with North Wexford one of the gems of Ireland's Ancient East. The development is convenient to bus routes, the M11 Motorway, cafés, shops, restaurants, schools and the popular Amber Springs Hotel and Leisure Club. Gorey is a modern town with a traditional feel. Its rich history as a market trading town is reflected today in the high number of local businesses and producers. \r\n\r\nThe region is abundant with everything from high fashion to authentic gourmet eateries, great places to stay, as well unlimited outdoor recreations, a thriving arts and culture community and plenty of pubs filled with live music and atmosphere, a bustling town to say the least!\r\n\r\nSurrounded by numerous top-level golf clubs, Gorey boasts a wide variety of activities from the historic Ferns to the seaside villages of Courtown and Ballymoney to the modern traditional market town of Gorey itself."
      },
